{"kind":"request","text":"J5: one room's \"needs you\", with the agent wake\n\nScope: plan 032 section 2b, J5, and section 2f, decision 3 (notes/plans/032-2026-10-17-journey-as-acceptance-target.md). S2, S3 and S4 have landed, and so has the Needs you view from S4 and the view design at notes/2026-10-17-journey-views-design.md. Start by stating what S4 already gives, and build only the gap.\n\nThe scene for a person: Ana is away for three days. A teammate asks her to approve something, and an agent waits on her decision. Ana comes back on a different device. She opens the room's \"needs you\" and sees every item that arrived, each with what needs her, why it is hers, and what will settle it. She reads one and it stays open. She marks the list reviewed, and the next visit shows what has changed since then.\n\nThe scene for an agent: an agent asks a person for a decision and stops. When the person decides, an authorized event feed from the room wakes the agent, with no webhook, and the agent resumes from the record.\n\nDone when each item names its rule and the act that settles it, reading an item leaves it open, an absent person returning on another device sees every item that arrived, and an agent that waits on a person is woken by the room's feed and resumes. Run the real user path for the witness, on a deployed Worker for the person's part. Schedules and webhook conditions come later.\n\nWrite a short design section first if the wake needs one, opening with the scene. If the wake needs hosted MCP open, name the Worker and the tool in the review request.\n\nOrder: after J2.","body":{"conditions":"Each needs-you item names its rule and settling act, reading leaves it open, an absent person on another device sees every item, and a waiting agent is woken by the room's feed and resumes, approved by the checker and landed on main.","target_head":"ad1ec31c06d199583d5100763f65618907942950","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572